# THE INPUT FILE. Edit THIS, never requirements.txt.
#
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file and pins the ENTIRE dependency
# tree, transitive packages included, for Linux AND Windows on Python >= 3.12.
# A floating transitive version moves results exactly as a direct one does, and
# every number in docs/ is only reproducible against the versions it was
# measured on. To add or upgrade a dependency, see "Dependencies" in CLAUDE.md
# section 8: edit this file, re-run tools/lock_requirements.ps1, commit both.
#
# Render installs requirements.txt and ONLY that. Nothing that the API does not
# import belongs here (torch's Phase 0 removal, and the arch/linearmodels split
# into requirements-evidence.in, are the two standing examples).
